Load the original stress helpers through Crawl's supported Lua loader.

CLua::init_lua deliberately does not open Lua's package library (clua.cc:
735-763), so global require is absent.  It registers crawl_require at line
826; that loader reports execution failures (1232-1250).  The production
Dungeon Lua scripts already use crawl_require, e.g. dat/dlua/dungeon.lua:6-8
and dat/dlua/debug.lua:6.

The inherited stress rc files still call the removed global require in four
places.  This leaves entomb/awaken setup inactive in the first two scenarios,
and fireworks reports nil require/stress before its later targeting prompt.
Use the supported loader at every affected call, restoring the original
helper execution without enabling unrestricted Lua libraries, changing the
helper code, suppressing errors, skipping scenarios, or changing timeouts.

--- a/crawl-ref/source/test/stress/fireworks.rc
+++ b/crawl-ref/source/test/stress/fireworks.rc
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 :     crawl.sendkeys("&" .. string.char(20) ..
 :                    "debug.disable('confirmations')" .. eol ..
 :                    "debug.disable('death')" .. eol ..
-:                    "require('dlua/stress.lua')" .. eol ..
+:                    "crawl_require('dlua/stress.lua')" .. eol ..
 :                    "stress.fill_level('floor')" .. eol ..
 :                    "you.teleport_to(40, 33)" .. eol ..
 :                    "dgn.create_monster(40, 40, 'statue hp:10000')" .. eol ..
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
 :     end
 :   end
 :   if (you.turns() % 7) == 1 then
-:     crawl.call_dlua("require('dlua/stress.lua')" .. eol ..
+:     crawl.call_dlua("crawl_require('dlua/stress.lua')" .. eol ..
 :                     "stress.boost_monster_hp()")
 :     crawl.sendkeys("&corb" .. eol .. eol)
 :   end
--- a/crawl-ref/source/test/stress/woken_rest.rc
+++ b/crawl-ref/source/test/stress/woken_rest.rc
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
 :     crawl.enable_more(false)
 :     crawl.set_sendkeys_errors(true)
 :     crawl.process_keys("&Y" .. esc)
-:     crawl.call_dlua("require('dlua/stress.lua');" ..
+:     crawl.call_dlua("crawl_require('dlua/stress.lua');" ..
